On Thu, 2019-10-31 at 09:40 -0700, Wenlong Gong wrote:
> That's definitely helpful! I have two questions here on the setting
> in inla.priors.used(result):
> 1. what is this prior for?
> section=[family]
> 	tag=[INLA.Data1] component=[gaussian]
> 		theta1:
> 			parameter=[log precision]
> 			prior=[loggamma]
> 			param=[1e+00, 5e-05]

This is the prior for the precision in the Gaussian likelihood.

> 2. I saw this group.theta1 in each of random effects: s1,s2,s3, s12,
> s23, s13, what is it for? is it the prior for the std of error term
> e1, e2, e3, i.e., e.sd <http://e.sd>?
> 		group.theta1:
> 			parameter=[logit correlation]
> 			prior=[normal]
> 			param=[0.0, 0.2]

normally, this is not in use, only if you define f(..., group=)

the issue is that its hard in the code to distinguish the case
this is not used and number of groups is 1 (or > 1). so, you can
just ignore it if you do not use it.

Best
H

